  "query_preview": "..\nA very quiet doldrum-like pattern is expected in the wake of Typhoon\nSinlaku as it pulls further away from the northern CNMI. Light to \ngentle southwest to west winds will slowly shift toward the east- \nnortheast early this coming week as trade winds become dominant, and\nstart to pick up toward the end of the week. In the meantime, light \nand variable winds are expected to develop for Guam and Rota tonight,\nthen Tinian and Saipan Sunday night behind the departing TY Sinlaku.\nIf there is enough clearing in the upper-level cloud deck and low- \nlevel moisture is sufficient, this may allow for afternoon island- \neffect showers to develop over Guam on Sunday. However, the current \nforecast indicates precipitable water amounts ranging 1.10 to 1.70 \ninches which is fairly dry for the tropics.",
